## Boundary

The host runtime verifies repository facts. The Sounio kernel does not parse Git
objects or recompute SHA-256. It consumes opaque tokens at that trust boundary
and enforces the state transition algebra:

```text
Preregistered + ancestry + distinct treatment/control artifacts -> Observed
Observed(PASS, PASS) -> Supported -> promotable
Observed(FAIL, PASS) -> Falsified -> retained, not promotable
Observed(_, FAIL) -> Inconclusive -> retained, not promotable
```

The state structs are private to their defining module. External code cannot
directly construct `SupportedExperiment`, and `promote_supported` accepts no other state.
This is a nominal protocol boundary, not a theorem that the opaque host inputs
are truthful.

## Falsification Conditions

- a failed sabotage control can produce `SupportedExperiment`;
- treatment and control can reuse one artifact identity;
- an observation can use the preregistration commit as its subject;
- external code can directly construct a supported state;
- a preregistered, falsified, or inconclusive state is accepted for promotion;
- disabling the support control guard does not change the negative witness.

